# adamfit: expression shapes fitted by Adam, priced, measured, the closest
# certified (src/adamfit.c).  Small budgets: count and steps keep it quick.
adamfit cos(x) in 0..1 count 160 steps 40 auto list 3
adamfit sin(x) in 0..0.5 count 100 steps 40 wcost 2 werr 0.2 list 2
fit exp(x) on 0..1 with adam count 100 steps 30 list 2 and just report the closest
adamfit x*y in 0..1 count 40 steps 20 auto list 1
adamfit p*q*r*s*t in 0..1
adamfit cos(x) in 0..1 ops sqrt
# integers: fixed-point forms, exact ones proved on every point
adamfit (x: u16) / 3 auto list 2
mul8(x: u8, y: u8) = u8((u16(x) * u16(y) + 127) / 255)
adamfit mul8 auto list 1 budget 300
# two float parameters, measured on independent uniform points
hyp(x: f32 in 0..1, y: f32 in 0..1) = sqrt(x*x + y*y)
adamfit hyp count 60 steps 30 auto list 1
# code, sampled natively: C (it lowers: its cost), GLSL's scalar subset
adamfit quant v in 0..4095 auto list 1
```c
#include <stdint.h>
uint32_t quant(uint32_t v) { return (v * 1000u) / 4095u; }
```
adamfit luma r in 0..255, g in 0..255 auto list 1 budget 300
```glsl
#version 450
uint luma(uint r, uint g)
{
    return (r * 77u + g * 150u + 64u) / 255u;
}
```
adamfit tonemap x in 0..4 count 120 steps 30 auto list 1
```glsl
float tonemap(float x)
{
    return clamp(x * (2.51 * x + 0.03) / (x * (2.43 * x + 0.59) + 0.14), 0.0, 1.0);
}
```
adamfit f
```glsl
vec2 f(vec2 p) { return p; }
```
